  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $a, b, c$ and $d$ be any four real numbers. Then. $a^{n}+b^{n}=c^{n}+d^{n}$ holds for any natural number $n$. if",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CWKD5",
      "text": "$a+b=c+d$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oaDlf",
      "text": "$a-b=c-d$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jOply",
      "text": "$a+b=c+d \\cdot d^{2}+b^{2}=c^{2}+d^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pzD1Q",
      "text": "$a-b=c-d \\cdot d^{2}-b^{2}=c^{2}-d^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "From option (d), we have <br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />a-b &=c-d \\\\<br />a^{2}-b^{2} &=c^{2}-d^{2}<br />\\end{aligned}$<br />Consider, $a^{2}-b^{2}=c^{2}-d^{2}$<br />$\\Rightarrow(a+b)(a-b)=(c-d)(c+d)$<br />$\\Rightarrow \\quad a+b=c+d$<br />On adding Eqs we get<br />$2 a=2 c \\Rightarrow a=c$<br />$\\Rightarrow \\quad b=d$<br />Thus, $a^{n}+b^{n}=c^{n}+d^{n}$ for all $n \\in N$",
    "image": null
  },
